  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When both of the inputs are given with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;that is logical <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, both of the diodes are in OFF condition and hence supply voltage will appear at the base terminal of the transistor which makes it switched ON and supply voltage gets a path to the ground through this transistors. Therefore, it represents NAND gate.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><menclose notation=\"top\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>B</mi></menclose></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
